@* What the osb team looks for in a showcased storyboard, next to the submit form.
   A first draft: change the wording to the team's own. *@
<section aria-labelledby="look-for-title" class="card p-6">
    <h2 id="look-for-title" class="section-title">What we look for</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mint-200">The showcase collects storyboards that make people stop and watch. We look for:</p>
    <ul class="mt-4 flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mint-200">
        <li><strong class="text-mint-50">An idea carried through.</strong> A story, a style or an effect that shapes the whole song, not just its best moment. The showcase tags, from Particles and Lyrics to 3D and Narrative, are some of the ways a storyboard stands out.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-mint-50">Timing.</strong> Movement, cuts and lyrics that land on the music and follow its mood.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-mint-50">A map that's still playable.</strong> Nothing that hides the notes, and an epilepsy warning when it strobes or flashes fast.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-mint-50">Smooth playback</strong> on an ordinary computer. osu!'s <a href="https://osu.ppy.sh/wiki/en/Ranking_criteria#storyboarding">storyboard rules</a> make a good checklist.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 border-t border-charcoal-600 pt-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-sage">It doesn't have to be ranked, or yours: you can suggest someone else's storyboard too.</p>
</section>
